course: dictionary
lesson: 2530
title: Official orders: decree
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A decree is an official order. It comes from a ruler, a government or a court, and people are expected to obey it. Context clues often show you when a decree is meant. «The Ems decree (1876) banned most publishing and stage performance in Ukrainian in the Russian Empire» tells you the decree was an order that stopped something.
explain: The word also works as a verb. To decree something is to order it officially, so «the king decreed» means the king gave an official order. Look for clues like issued, ordered, banned or by royal decree. These words tell you a decree is a serious order, not just a suggestion.
explain: Decree can also mean a court's decision. A judge may sign a divorce decree, which is an official court decision. Here the word is still about an official decision that must be followed.
fact: A decree is an official order given by a ruler, a government or a court.
fact: To decree something is to order it officially.
fact: «Caesar Augustus sent out a decree that everyone must be counted» in the Bible, which is why Mary and Joseph went to Bethlehem.
fact: A court can also give a decree, such as a divorce decree.
fact: Useful phrases are «issue a decree», «by royal decree» and «decree that».
exercise: «The king issued a decree that every village must build a well.» What is a decree? | A spoken joke | A kind of tree that grows in the hills | A sad song sung at a feast | *An official order given by a ruler
exercise: «The mayor decreed that the park would stay open late.» Find and copy the word that means ordered officially. | open | late | *decreed | park
exercise: Which of these is most like a decree? | A list of your favourite foods | A birthday card from a friend | A cloud that looks like a dog | *A law written down by the government
test: Which word means a court's official decision, such as a divorce decree? | Decoy | *Decree | Decay | Degree
test: «In the Bible, Caesar Augustus sent out a decree that everyone must be counted.» What did the decree say? | Everyone must go to the sea | Everyone must sing | Everyone must eat bread | *Everyone must be counted
exam: «The ruler decreed that every child must learn to read.» Which word tells you the ruler gave an official order? | *decreed | ruler | learn | child
